# Everything a user's own installation produces stays on their machine.
#
# The failure this file exists to prevent is someone committing their own registry - the projects
# they work on, the tickets they were given, the briefs and reports those produced. Anything
# written at run time belongs below, and a new run-time directory belongs here before its first
# write, not after someone notices it in a diff.

# The King's own standing instructions. Stated by hand, read by the Hand, never edited by it,
# and never shared. instructions.example.md is the tracked template the installer copies.
/instructions.md

# The durable work state: the project registry, the backlog, per-work briefs and reports, and
# the two curated memory files.
/data/

# Live worker records.
/state/

# Per-installation configuration: the startup-memory budget, the ADO organization and project,
# and anything else with one right answer per machine.
/config/

# Third-party binaries dropped in by hand - the review gate lives here.
/tools/

# Rendered review surfaces, wherever they land.
*.review.html

# Git worktrees created by dispatch.
.claude/worktrees/

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
